## What changed

- `src/links.ts`
  - An **overload signature** now resolves to the body written beside it (same symbol, same parent), so `Auth.header(...)` reaches its implementation and its `callers` lists both namespace calls.
  - A **`new`** of a local class now names the class declaration, not the inherited `Error` construct signature.
  - A member taken from a **factory value** (`yield* Steps.make(...)` → `steps.attempt(...)`) follows the shorthand property to the variable that holds the written function.
  - **Returned object literals** are implementation candidates (expected type or the literal’s own type), so a `Transport` implementation returned from `fileTransport()` is found.
- `src/project.ts` — real paths decide repository source: workspace packages linked under `node_modules` are included and reported by their real paths; real dependencies are still excluded. Root and `sourceOf` are real-path aware too.
- `src/siblings.ts` — sibling rows compare exported `Effect.fn`/arrow constants as well as function declarations.
- `src/commands.ts` — an empty sibling table now states why; a map of some paths carries a limit naming the caller folders it did not search.

